## (1) Five of My Favorite Cat Facts

| # | Fact | Why It’s Cool |
|---|------|---------------|
| 1 | **Cats have a “right‑ing” reflex** | When a cat falls, it can twist its body in mid‑air to land on its feet—thanks to a highly flexible spine and a vestibular system that senses orientation. |
| 2 | **They can make over 100 different sounds** | While dogs have about 10, cats can produce a wide range of vocalizations—meows, purrs, chirps, hisses, and even a “trill” that’s used to greet humans. |
| 3 | **Their whiskers are touch‑sensitive “sensors”** | Whiskers detect changes in the air and help cats gauge whether they can fit through tight spaces. They’re so sensitive that a single breeze can trigger a cat’s curiosity. |
| 4 | **Cats have a “third eye”—the tapetum lucidum** | This reflective layer behind the retina amplifies light, giving cats excellent night vision and that iconic glowing eye effect in photos. |
| 5 | **They can “talk” to humans** | Studies show that cats adjust their meows to be more human‑like when they’re trying to get attention or food—almost as if they’re learning to communicate with us. |

